    {
      "paperId": "/article/10.1007/s12083-022-01361-0",
      "doi": "10.1007/s12083-022-01361-0",
      "title": "A regional interest-aware caching placement scheme for reducing latency in the LEO satellite networks",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Liu Zhiguo, Li Weijie, ... Li Yunqi"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2022,
      "abstract": "In view of the large response time delay of content placement in ICN satellite network, considering the regional characteristics of content and user's interest preference, a cache placement strategy for LEO satellite network based on regional interest perception is proposed, which takes into account the balanced distribution of content and reduces the response time delay. Firstly, the label of content is used as the distance measure of content similarity, and the whole network content is divided into multiple content clusters by a clustering algorithm. Secondly, according to the historical request data, the interest preference of the content cluster is evaluated, so as to divide the cache space of the whole network content. Finally, taking the average time delay as the optimization objective, the greedy algorithm is used to solve the problem of optimal placement of content. Simulation results show that the proposed method is superior to the comparison method in content response delay and cache hit rate.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "In view of the large response time delay of content placement in ICN satellite network, considering the regional characteristics of content and...",
