    {
      "paperId": "/article/10.1007/s42405-022-00508-w",
      "doi": "10.1007/s42405-022-00508-w",
      "title": "Causality-Seq2Seq Model for Battery Anomaly Detection",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Hyungseok Shin, Juhee Lee, Phil Kim"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2022,
      "abstract": "Battery anomalies are critical problems directly related to the safety of battery-powered devices such as electric vehicles and drones, since battery anomalies often lead immediately to critical failures. This study proposes a method to detect battery anomalies in real time using an unsupervised deep learning model. The proposed method detects battery anomalies using a strong correlation existing between the battery’s voltage and current based on a sequence-to-sequence (Seq2Seq)-type deep learning model. The performance of the proposed method was validated through the drone’s flight data. The proposed method in this study exhibited superior anomaly detection performance compared to conventional prediction-based and reconstruction-based anomaly detection models.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "Battery anomalies are critical problems directly related to the safety of battery-powered devices such as electric vehicles and drones, since battery...",
